34,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Oh dear, it seems our hardworking friends in the lab are quite overwhelmed. We must be very careful not to add to their burden.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"As I suspected. Our ""good faith"" approvals are meaningless if the paperwork doesn't align with the shipping deadlines. We've been failing at the basics.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"Well, this is a bit of a wake-up call. It turns out our ""prestigious"" static displays are actually quite boring for the public.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The building is struggling. The suspended bay has a strict weight limit, and the powered displays are causing too many failures.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,I found them! The money-monsters are the trucks and the fancy stands! They're eating all the coins!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, that sounds quite worrying. We wouldn't want any accidents. Perhaps a simpler exhibition would be kinder to the building and the staff.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Sakura, costs are a symptom, not the cause. The cause is a lack of logistical discipline. We need a proposal that is lean and easy to transport.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shion, ""lean"" usually means ""boring."" The visitors want something alive. They want people, they want movement. They're tired of staring at glass boxes.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, movement is exactly the problem. The powered displays are unreliable and the floor cannot support heavy, static installations.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"But if we use things that don't need fancy stands, we can spend the money on something fun! Like... ice cream! Just kidding!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I am worried that we are planning for a museum that exists only on paper. Our volunteers are already busy elsewhere.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Let's be logical. We need a candidate that doesn't require complex shipping, doesn't overload the bay, and doesn't rely on failing electronics.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"And it has to be something that actually brings people back. If we just do another ""safe"" show, we're just wasting the space.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,I cannot support any proposal that involves heavy stonework or complex machinery. The risk of a structural failure or a blackout is too high.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Sakura,,I agree with @Shion! Let's pick the one that doesn't cost a million dollars just to move it from the truck to the wall!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
