60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,I believe Option A is the most gentle choice. It uses local people and doesn't seem to demand too much from our tired staff.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is the only logical choice. Local sourcing eliminates the shipping cut-off risks and minimizes transport costs. It's the only safe bet.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"I'm torn, but Option B is actually quite exciting. A working conservation bench? That's exactly the kind of ""human"" element that brings people back.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option C is out of the question; the rigging and powered displays are too risky. Option B's reconstructions might be too heavy for the bay.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Option A! It's local! No big trucks, no scary invoices, and no money-monsters! It's the winner!","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, a working bench sounds lovely, but I fear for the conservation staff. They are already so far behind in their work.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@May, Option B still involves municipal digs and potentially heavy artifacts. Option A is the only one that guarantees we won't be apologizing at the door.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, if the staff are on display, it might actually make their work more appreciated! But @Shion is right about the ""safe"" part. Maybe A is the way.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, the conservation lab is already backlogged. Adding a public-facing bench would only slow them down further. Option A is the most stable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Sakura,,See? Everyone likes Option A! It's like a big party with local friends!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I feel a great sense of relief that we are considering the well-being of our team. Option A is a very kind choice.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"It is not about kindness, Shizue; it is about efficiency. Option A removes the variables that have caused us to fail in the past.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"I still love the idea of B, but I can't argue with the data. If we want people to come back, the ""demonstration sessions"" in A will do the trick.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,Option A is the only one that doesn't threaten the structural integrity of the gallery or the stability of the power grid.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Sakura,,Yay! We all agree! No more money-monsters!,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
